en-US.quiz-maker.usage:
**What it does**: generates questions from knowledge-base documents, turning what you've read into checkable practice.

**How to use** (pick any of three):
1. Tell Baize: "Make 5 questions from 'Document name'", "Give me a set of fill-in-the-blanks" — the question officer writes to spec and in depth (every question passes grounding checks + blind-answer validation); the practice view opens automatically when done;
2. Agent panel "Study" tab → click "Generate questions" to go straight there;
3. Wrong or unsure questions enter SM-2 review scheduling; "Today's review" on the Study tab walks you through them on schedule; the practice page shows per-question mastery and health (down-vote rate / validation share); retired questions can be restored in place.

**Notes**: "Single choice · warm-up" is generated deterministically (no LLM cost); in-depth questions are written by the question officer and pass a double quality gate.

